Q29. Reusable Grade Function
Create a function that accepts marks and returns a grade. Keep input validation separate
from grade calculation.

Q30. Prime Function
Write isPrime(number), returning a Boolean. Reuse it to print all primes in a range.

Q31. Palindrome Function
Write a function that checks whether a string is a palindrome. Decide whether spaces,
punctuation, and letter case should be ignored, and document your choice.

Q32. Recursive Factorial
Calculate factorial using recursion. Explain the base case and test what happens when the
base case is missing.

Q33. Array Statistics
Write functions to calculate sum, average, smallest value, and largest value without using
built-in sum/min/max shortcuts. Decide how empty arrays should be handled.

Q34. Password Strength Checker
Write a function that checks length, uppercase, lowercase, digit, and special-character
requirements. Return useful feedback rather than only true/false.

