SECTION D — STRINGS
============================================================

Q35. Reverse a String
Reverse a string without using the built-in reverse() method. Compare a loop-based approach
with an approach that uses an array.

Q36. Character Frequency
Count how many times each character occurs in a string. Decide how to treat uppercase and
lowercase characters.

Q37. Vowel and Consonant Counter
Count vowels and consonants in a sentence. Ignore spaces, digits, and punctuation.

Q38. Word Counter
Count words in a sentence with extra spaces at the beginning, end, or between words.

Q39. Anagram Checker
Determine whether two strings are anagrams. Decide how spaces, punctuation, and case are
handled and test your decision.

Q40. First Non-Repeating Character
Find the first character that appears only once. Define the result when every character repeats.

Q41. Remove Duplicate Characters
Remove repeated characters while preserving the first occurrence order. Example: banana
becomes ban.

Q42. Find the Longest Word
Find the longest word in a sentence. Decide how punctuation should be treated and what to
return for an empty sentence.

============================================================
SECTION E — ARRAYS AND DATA LOGIC
============================================================

Q43. Remove Duplicates
Create a new array with duplicate values removed while preserving original order. First solve
without Set, then compare your approach with Set.

Q44. Frequency of Array Values
Count the occurrences of each value in an array and display the frequency table.

Q45. Rotate an Array
Rotate an array to the right by K positions. Handle K larger than the array length and empty
arrays.

Q46. Move Zeros to the End
Move every zero to the end while preserving the order of non-zero elements. Try to do this
without creating a second array.

Q47. Merge Two Sorted Arrays
Merge two already-sorted arrays into one sorted array without calling sort().

Q48. Missing Number
An array contains distinct numbers from 1 through N with one number missing. Find the missing
number and explain the time and space complexity of your approach.

Q49. Two-Sum
Given an array and a target, find two distinct elements whose sum equals the target. Return
their indices or clearly state when no pair exists.

Q50. Transaction Analyzer
Given an array of transaction amounts, calculate total income, total expenses, net balance,
largest transaction, and average transaction amount. Define how positive, negative, and zero
amounts are interpreted.

