SECTION F — CLI PROJECTS (BUILD THESE AFTER THE QUESTIONS)
============================================================

PROJECT 1 — Student Management CLI
Features:
- Add a student with ID, name, and marks.
- List all students.
- Search by ID.
- Update student details.
- Delete a student.
- Calculate each student's average and grade.
- Prevent duplicate IDs and validate marks.
- Show a menu until the user chooses Exit.
Stretch goal: save and load data from a JSON file.

PROJECT 2 — ATM Simulator
Features:
- PIN check with a limited number of attempts.
- View balance.
- Deposit money.
- Withdraw money with balance and amount validation.
- Show a transaction history.
- Exit safely.
Stretch goal: separate account logic into functions and maintain a transaction log.

PROJECT 3 — Inventory and Billing System
Features:
- Add, update, search, and remove products.
- Store product ID, name, price, and stock quantity.
- Create a customer bill from selected products and quantities.
- Prevent selling more items than are in stock.
- Calculate subtotal, discount, and final amount.
Stretch goal: low-stock warnings and JSON persistence.

PROJECT 4 — Employee Payroll CLI
Features:
- Add and list employees.
- Store employee ID, name, basic salary, and allowances.
- Calculate gross salary and deductions using documented rules.
- Search, update, and delete employee records.
- Validate all numeric inputs.
Stretch goal: monthly payroll summary and export to a text or JSON report.

PROJECT 5 — Quiz Application
Features:
- Store questions and multiple-choice options.
- Ask questions one by one.
- Validate answers.
- Track score and percentage.
- Display correct answers after submission.
- Allow replay.
Stretch goal: shuffle questions and show a high-score table.

PROJECT 6 — Personal Expense Tracker
Features:
- Add income and expense transactions.
- Categorize transactions.
- List transactions and filter by category.
- Calculate total income, expenses, and balance.
- Show the largest expense and spending by category.
Stretch goal: monthly summaries and JSON persistence.

PROJECT 7 — Contact Book
Features:
- Add, view, search, edit, and delete contacts.
- Store name, phone, email, and optional address.
- Search by partial name or phone number.
- Validate required fields and prevent accidental duplicate contacts.
Stretch goal: sort contacts alphabetically and save/load JSON data.

